WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
Now to this.

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.268
There are questions surrounding Senator

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.303
Dianne Feinstein

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.671
after her brief exchange

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.573
yesterday with reporters on the Hill.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.907
The Democrat recently returned

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.175
after an extended absence

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:09.843
from Capitol Hill

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.444
recovering from shingles.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.413
So a reporter asked the 89 year

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.114
old lawmaker

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.982
how she's been received by her colleagues

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.550
since she returned to Washington.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.785
Let me read you the exchange.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.820
It was not on camera but here it is,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.622
verbatim quote.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.524
What have I heard about what

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.760
she asked about your return?

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:27.794
The reporter replied,

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.662
I haven't been gone, she said.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.263
You should.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.465
I haven't been gone. I have been working.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.167
You've been working from home.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.101
Is that what you're saying?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.002
The reporter asked.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.737
No, I've been here.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.805
I've been voting.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.874
Please either know or don't know.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:41.741
Close quote.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.642
CNN has reached out

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.077
to find an office for comment.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:44.778
No word back.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.447
But joining us now is Benjamin Oreskes.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.681
He is one of the reporters

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.550
that asked those questions.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:50.984
He's a reporter

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.185
for The Los Angeles Times.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.587
So you were there? We weren't there.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.356
Is there a nuance missed in

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.090
what I just read

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.060
I mean.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.762
No, I think that

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.864
given the ample amount of reporting

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.232
that we've seen in outlets

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.400
like my outlet,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.401
San Francisco Chronicle,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.536
the New Yorker about,

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.304
you know, her memory loss,

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.339
her struggles to keep up,

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.641
you know, an intense schedule

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.376
that a senator requires.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.510
You know, we felt it was important

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.678
to put this out into the world.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:19.312
You know, obviously,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:19.946
there's a charitable

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.814
interpretation of this

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.449
and she's been back for a week.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.850
Maybe she thought I was,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.585
you know, talking about the last week.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.053
But, you know, given

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.221
what has been reported

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.389
and had been reported

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.990
over the last couple of years,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.259
it sort of seemed in line with that.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.494
And, you know,

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.129
this is someone who

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.298
whose absence was felt

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.166
deeply by her colleagues,

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.501
partially because they're close to her

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:41.868
and also

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.570
because it made the work of government

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.371
more difficult and sort of

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.340
seen her in one of the brief moments

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.475
she's been pretty shielded

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.209
from reporters.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:49.442
You know,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.877
we were trying to show what she is

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:51.678
like right now.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:52.879
We don't get a lot of opportunities

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.013
to hear her talk.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.515
This was important for that reason.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.416
Did her office

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:57.317
say anything

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.952
after this exchange happened?

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.720
Did they try to clarify

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.488
what she was saying?

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.489
Have you heard anything from them?

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.192
I know there's a short answer.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.427
We reached out to them.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:07.694
You know,

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.562
we told them what we were going to say.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.097
We all have audio of it.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.332
And, you know,

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.600
there were multiple staffers

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.001
with her at that moment

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.936
and they had nothing to say after,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.872
you know, after we went to them.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.373
Senator Blumenthal

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.875
has been a really vocal voice,

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:22.976
speaking in support of her

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.344
in her return, saying essentially

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.379
she's fully capable of doing her jobs.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.047
I wonder if you're hearing the same

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:28.915
from the rest of her

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:32.619
Democratic colleagues in private.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:33.419
It's a mix.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:34.821
I mean, obviously, you know,

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.289
we have been reporting on this story

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:36.990
from D.C.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.091
and from California,

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:38.424
where there's

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.759
an incredible amount of anxiety.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.362
We have to remember, her seat is open

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:43.396
You know, people are three

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.130
people are running,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.399
three prominent Democrats are running

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:50.403
it definitely from her colleagues in D.C.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.338
They are confident that she can vote

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.773
and they're happy to have her back.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:54.607
And they sort of

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.576
say she's the master of her own fate.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:57.210
She's in control

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.144
of her own health decisions.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.646
And if she feels like she's healthy,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.747
she she should be here

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.350
Benjamin Oreskes, thank you very much.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.618
And you said you have the audio, right,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.386
so people could go

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.887
and listen for themselves.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.821
Okay. Yeah.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.055
All right.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.323
We'll try to play that for people later.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.091
Thank you very much for joining.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:12.992
We have new audio

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.160
that we just got into CNN.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.929
And it is from The L.A. Times.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:18.231
It's an exchange between a few reporters

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.433
and Senator Dianne Feinstein,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.801
the Democratic senator recently

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.102
returned to Capitol Hill

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.038
after an extended absence

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:27.840
that drew a lot of scrutiny and criticism

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.008
even from some of her colleagues

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.010
as she was recovering from shingles

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.878
Given the key role

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.779
she plays on the Senate

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:33.947
Judiciary Committee

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:35.481
and confirming judges,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.550
a reporter asked the 89 year old lawmaker

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.752
how she's been received by her colleagues

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.988
since she got back to Washington.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:42.956
This is what she said

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.392
What have you heard?

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.460
What have I heard about

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.529
what about your return,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:50.296
how they felt about,

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.198
you know, why we haven't been gone.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:52.966
Okay.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.101
You should follow me.

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.136
I haven't been going. I've been working.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.004
You've been working from

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.005
home, is what you're saying.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.506
I've been here

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.277
I've been voting.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:07.580
You know, we don't know, because

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.083
in our last hour, we spoke with the L.A.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:10.817
Times reporter

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:11.985
that Senator Feinstein

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.353
was speaking with there.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.854
He said that she was back for a week

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:15.455
at that point,

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:16.556
and that may have been

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.258
what she was referring to.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:18.558
Of course,

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.492
it raised a lot of questions,

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.493
given she was gone for two

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.661
and a half months.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.595
CNN has reached out

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.730
to Feinstein's office

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.098
for a comment on their version

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.833
of what happened in this exchange.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:27.767
No word back yet.

